       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2,000 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** This could cause hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg orally three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg orally four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the standard maximum)\n- **650 mg orally every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you do want 2000 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, tell me which regimen to use and I'll enter it."
      }
